.TH RAZER-CLI 1 "2026-09-01" "razer-cli 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
razer-cli \- control fans, power modes and RGB keyboard of Razer laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B razer-cli
.RB [ \-\-source
.IR ac|bat ]
.I command
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B razer-cli
controls Razer laptop hardware directly over USB HID feature reports.
No kernel module, no daemon, and no GUI are required.
It can manage fan speed, power modes, keyboard backlighting, logo LED state,
and the battery health optimizer.
.PP
Settings are persisted in a JSON configuration file at
.IR ~/.local/share/razercontrol/config.json .
The
.B restore
command reapplies saved settings at any time or can be invoked at boot via
the included systemd user service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-source " " \fIac\fR|\fIbat\fR
Target a specific power profile.
If omitted, the profile is auto-detected from
.IR /sys/class/power_supply/AC/online .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS read
Read the current value of an attribute from hardware or configuration.
.TP
.B read fan
Print the current fan speed.
Returns \fBAuto (0)\fR when the fan is in automatic mode,
the RPM value when running manually, or \fBUnknown\fR on error.
.TP
.B read power
Print the current power mode (Balanced, Gaming, Creator, Silent, or Custom).
When in Custom mode (4), also prints the CPU and GPU boost levels.
.TP
.B read brightness
Print the current keyboard backlight brightness as a percentage (0\-100).
.TP
.B read logo
Print the current logo LED state (Off, On, or Breathing).
Read from the saved configuration.
.TP
.B read sync
Print whether AC and battery lighting profiles are synced (true/false).
.TP
.B read bho
Print the battery health optimizer state (on/off and threshold percentage).
Returns an error message if the model does not support BHO.
.SS write
Write a new value.
Changes are saved to the configuration and applied to hardware immediately
when targeting the active power state.
.TP
.BR write fan " \-\-speed \fIRPM\fR"
Set the fan speed.
Use \fB0\fR for automatic control, or any positive integer for manual RPM.
.TP
.BR write power " \-\-power \fIMODE\fR"
Set the power mode.
Modes:
.RS
.IP 0 4
Balanced
.IP 1 4
Gaming
.IP 2 4
Creator
.IP 3 4
Silent
.IP 4 4
Custom (requires \-\-cpu and \-\-gpu)
.RE
.TP
.BR write power " \-\-power 4 \-\-cpu \fILEVEL\fR \-\-gpu \fILEVEL\fR"
Set a custom power mode with explicit CPU and GPU boost levels.
CPU boost: 0=Low, 1=Medium, 2=High, 3=Boost (model-dependent).
GPU boost: 0=Low, 1=Medium, 2=High.
Both \fB\-\-cpu\fR and \fB\-\-gpu\fR are required when power mode is 4.
.TP
.BR write brightness " \-\-brightness \fIPCT\fR"
Set the keyboard backlight brightness.
.I PCT
must be between 0 and 100.
If sync is enabled, the value is mirrored to the other power profile.
.TP
.BR write logo " \-\-state \fIVALUE\fR"
Set the logo LED mode.
States:
.RS
.IP 0 4
Off
.IP 1 4
On
.IP 2 4
Breathing
.RE
If sync is enabled, the value is mirrored to the other power profile.
.TP
.BR write sync " \-\-state " \fIon\fR|\fIoff\fR"
Enable or disable syncing of lighting settings (brightness, logo)
between AC and battery profiles.
.TP
.BR write bho " \-\-state " \fIon\fR|\fIoff\fR
Enable or disable the battery health optimizer.
.TP
.BR write bho " \-\-state on \-\-threshold \fIVALUE\fR"
Enable BHO with a specific charging threshold.
.I VALUE
must be a multiple of 5 between 50 and 80.
.SS effect
Set a firmware keyboard lighting effect.
The chosen effect is saved to the configuration and restored on reboot via
.BR "razer-cli restore" .
.TP
.B effect off
Turn off keyboard backlighting.
.TP
.B effect spectrum
Enable spectrum cycling effect (cycles through all colors).
.TP
.BR effect wave " \-\-direction \fIDIR\fR"
Enable the wave effect.
.I DIR
is \fB0\fR (left\-to\-right) or \fB1\fR (right\-to\-left).
.TP
.BR effect reactive " \-\-speed \fISPD\fR " \-\-red \fIR\fR " \-\-green \fIG\fR " \-\-blue \fIB\fR"
Enable the reactive effect.
.I SPD
(0\-255) controls animation speed.
.IR R ,\  G ,\  B
(0\-255 each) set the color.
.TP
.BR effect static " \-\-red \fIR\fR " \-\-green \fIG\fR " \-\-blue \fIB\fR"
Set a static solid color on the keyboard.
.IR R ,\  G ,\  B
are RGB values from 0 to 255.
.TP
.BR effect breathing " \-\-kind \fIK\fR " [breathing options]
Enable the breathing effect.
.I KIND
selects the breathing mode:
.RS
.IP 0 4
Single color (uses red1/green1/blue1)
.IP 1 4
Dual color (uses red1/green1/blue1 and red2/green2/blue2)
.IP 2 4
Random color
.RE
.TP
.BR effect breathing " \-\-kind 0\-2 " \-\-red1 \fIR1\fR " \-\-green1 \fIG1\fR " \-\-blue1 \fIB1\fR " \-\-red2 \fIR2\fR " \-\-green2 \fIG2\fR " \-\-blue2 \fIB2\fR"
Full breathing options with both color slots (0\-255 per channel).
.TP
.BR effect starlight " \-\-kind \fIK\fR " \-\-speed \fISPD\fR " [starlight options]
Enable the starlight effect.
.I KIND
selects the mode:
.RS
.IP 0 4
Single color
.IP 1 4
Dual color
.IP 2 4
Random color
.RE
.IR SPD " (0\-255) controls animation speed."
.TP
.BR effect starlight " \-\-kind 0\-2 " \-\-speed \fISPD\fR " \-\-red1 \fIR1\fR " \-\-green1 \fIG1\fR " \-\-blue1 \fIB1\fR " \-\-red2 \fIR2\fR " \-\-green2 \fIG2\fR " \-\-blue2 \fIB2\fR"
Full starlight options with both color slots (0\-255 per channel).
.SS restore
Apply the saved configuration for the current power state.
This re-applies power mode, fan speed, brightness, logo state, and the
last keyboard effect.
Typically used at boot (via the systemd user service) or after a suspend cycle.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/razercontrol/config.json
Persistent configuration storing power profiles, sync flag, and last effect.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Device not found, hardware communication error, or invalid arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set fan to 3000 RPM on battery:
.PP
.RS
.nf
razer-cli --source bat write fan --speed 3000
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set custom power mode with high CPU and medium GPU:
.PP
.RS
.nf
razer-cli write power --power 4 --cpu 2 --gpu 1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set static red keyboard color at 80% brightness:
.PP
.RS
.nf
razer-cli effect static --red 255 --green 0 --blue 0
razer-cli write brightness --brightness 80
.fi
.RE
.PP
Enable battery health optimizer at 80% threshold:
.PP
.RS
.nf
razer-cli write bho --state on --threshold 80
.fi
.RE
.PP
Restore saved settings (e.g., at boot):
.PP
.RS
.nf
razer-cli restore
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
Maintained by MkDierz.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
